xt":"களைந்","tr":"kaḷain"}]},{"text":"தனவே","tr":"taṉavē","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"தன","tr":"taṉa"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வே","tr":"vē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"வயலை","parts":[{"text":"வயலை","lemma":"வயலை","gloss":"vayalai spinach/creeper"}],"gloss":"vayalai creeper"},{"surface":"கொடியின்","parts":[{"text":"கொடி","lemma":"கொடி","gloss":"creeper/vine"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"like/of"}],"gloss":"like a vine"},{"surface":"வாடிய","parts":[{"text":"வாடு","lemma":"வாடு","gloss":"wither"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"withered"},{"surface":"மருங்கின்","parts":[{"text":"மருங்கு","lemma":"மருங்கு","gloss":"waist/side"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of the waist"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உயவல்","parts":[{"text":"உயவு","lemma":"உயவு","gloss":"suffer/languish"},{"text":"அல்","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"nominalizing suffix"}],"gloss":"distressed / slow-moving"},{"surface":"ஊர்தி","parts":[{"text":"ஊர்தி","lemma":"ஊர்தி","gloss":"vehicle/mount"}],"gloss":"mount"},{"surface":"பயலை","parts":[{"text":"பயலை","lemma":"பயலை","gloss":"paleness/sallowness"}],"gloss":"pale-complexioned"},{"surface":"பார்ப்பான்","parts":[{"text":"பார்ப்பான்","lemma":"பார்ப்பான்","gloss":"Brahmin"}],"gloss":"Brahmin"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எல்லி","parts":[{"text":"எல்லி","lemma":"எல்லி","gloss":"night"}],"gloss":"at night"},{"surface":"வந்து","parts":[{"text":"வந்து","lemma":"வந்து","gloss":"having come"}],"gloss":"having come","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நில்லாது","parts":[{"text":"நில்","lemma":"நில்","gloss":"stand/stop"},{"text":"ஆது","lemma":"ஆது","gloss":"without (negative participle)"}],"gloss":"without stopping"},{"surface":"புக்கு","parts":[{"text":"புக்கு","lemma":"புக்கு","gloss":"having entered"}],"gloss":"having entered","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சொல்லிய","parts":[{"text":"சொல்","lemma":"சொல்","gloss":"speak"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"spoken"},{"surface":"சொல்லோ","parts":[{"text":"சொல்","lemma":"சொல்","gloss":"word"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ஓ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"words indeed"},{"surface":"சிலவே","parts":[{"text":"சில","lemma":"சில","gloss":"few"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"were few indeed"},{"surface":"அதற்கே","parts":[{"text":"அதற்கே","lemma":"அதற்கே","gloss":"for that itself"}],"gloss":"for that itself","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஏணியும்","parts":[{"text":"ஏணி","lemma":"ஏணி","gloss":"ladder"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the ladders"},{"surface":"சீப்பும்","parts":[{"text":"சீப்பு","lemma":"சீப்பு","gloss":"defensive gate-bolt/barrier"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the defensive barriers"},{"surface":"மாற்றி","parts":[{"text":"மாற்று","lemma":"மாற்று","gloss":"change/remove/turn back"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having removed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மாண்வினை","parts":[{"text":"மாண்","lemma":"மாண்","gloss":"excellent/glorious"},{"text":"வினை","lemma":"வினை","gloss":"action/work"}],"gloss":"of excellent deeds"},{"surface":"யானையும்","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"யானை","gloss":"elephant"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and/even"}],"gloss":"even the elephants"},{"surface":"மணி","parts":[{"text":"மணி","lemma":"மணி","gloss":"bell"}],"gloss":"bells"},{"surface":"களைந்தனவே","parts":[{"text":"களைந்தனவே","lemma":"களைந்தனவே","gloss":"were removed indeed"}],"gloss":"were removed indeed","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Like a vayalai vine withered waist / distressed mount pale Brahmin / at night having come, without stopping, having entered / spoken words indeed were few, for that itself / ladders and defensive barriers having removed / excellent-deeded elephants even bells were removed.","translation":"With a waist as thin as a withered vayalai vine, riding a slow, weary mount, the pale Brahmin arrived in the dark of night, entered without stopping, and spoke only a very few words. Yet, because of those few words, the siege ladders and defensive barriers were turned back, and the bells were stripped from the war-elephants of glorious deeds.","modern":"வாடிய வயலைக் கொடியைப் போன்ற மெலிந்த இடையையும், மெதுவாகச் செல்லும் வாகனத்தையும், வெளுத்த உடலையும் உடைய பார்ப்பான், இரவில் வந்து, எங்கும் நில்லாமல் நேராக உள்ளே நுழைந்து, சில சொற்களைத்தான் பேசினான். அவன் பேசிய அந்தச் சில சொற்களுக்காகவே, கோட்டையை முற்றுகையிட வைத்திருந்த ஏணிகளும் கதவுக் கணைய மரங்களும் அகற்றப்பட்டன; சிறந்த போர்த் தொழிலைச் செய்யும் யானைகளின் கழுத்து மணிகளும் அவிழ்த்து விடப்பட்டன.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Vākai tiṇai and specifically the Pārppaṉa vākai tuṟai, which celebrates the victory or excellence of a Brahmin mediator. The poet Madurai Vēḷācāṉ describes a frail, pale Brahmin messenger who travels on a slow, weary mount to negotiate peace between warring kings. He arrives in the middle of the night and enters the camp directly without hesitation. Though he speaks only a few words, his diplomatic skill is so powerful that the entire siege is called off. The ladders meant for scaling the fort walls and the defensive barriers are dismantled, and the bells are removed from the war-elephants, signaling the end of hostilities. The contrast between the messenger's weak physical appearance and the massive political impact of his brief words highlights the power of peaceful diplomacy over military might.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}